# {{project.title}}

AWS Cognito user pool for {{poolSettings.friendlyName}}, managed with CDK.

## Setup

- `pnpm install`
- `pnpm test`

## Deploying

Bitbucket deploys each environment with a manual trigger on `main`. Each deploy prints these stack
outputs, which the app projects need:

| Output | Used by |
| --- | --- |
| `Issuer` | API `jwt.issuer`; React `VITE_APP_COGNITO_AUTHORITY` |
| `Issuer` + `/.well-known/jwks.json` | API `jwt.jwksUri` |
| `SpaClientId` | API `jwt.clientIds`; React `VITE_APP_COGNITO_CLIENT_ID` |
| `HostedDomain` | React `VITE_APP_COGNITO_DOMAIN` |
| `ApiScope` | React `VITE_APP_COGNITO_SCOPE` (`openid email profile`, plus `ApiScope` if the API checks scopes; the starter API does not) |
| `UserPoolArn` | API CDK `userPoolArn` |

Cognito domain prefixes are unique per region across all of AWS. If a deploy fails because the
prefix is taken, change `domainPrefix` in `src/env-*.ts`.

## Email

The first deploy creates an SES identity for {{poolSettings.fromAddress}}, and AWS emails that address
a verification link. Until it is clicked, keep `useSes: false`; Cognito then sends email itself
(a few messages a day). After verifying, set `useSes: true` in the env file and deploy again.

The SES identity is created by the first environment's stack (staging when there is one). Deleting
that stack removes the identity the other environment uses.

New AWS accounts start in the SES sandbox and can only email verified addresses. Request production
access in the SES console before inviting real users.

## App URLs

Callback and logout URLs live in each `src/env-*.ts`. They must match the app's origin exactly,
with no trailing slash.

## Users

Self sign-up is off. Invite users from the Cognito console or the CLI. Mark the email as verified,
otherwise password reset does not work:

```bash
aws cognito-idp admin-create-user --user-pool-id <UserPoolId> --username <email> --user-attributes Name=email,Value=<email> Name=email_verified,Value=true --desired-delivery-mediums EMAIL
```

Put administrators in the `admin` group; the group appears in the access token's `cognito:groups` claim.

## Deleting

The user pool is kept when the stack is deleted, so users are not lost by accident. Delete it by
hand in the console if it really should go.
